#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""C22 VI-1/VI-2 (copy offload vs fault reduction, E4 and E5) and IV-4 (GraphBFS repeated staging). Reads gate_e/e4/mechanism.csv and e5/mechanism.csv; counter semantics cited from driver/src-e3a/uvm_gpu_replayable_faults.c.
Writes consolidation/C22_VI1_DECOMPOSITION.md and C22_IV4_GRAPHBFS.md."""
import csv
rd = lambda p: list(csv.DictReader(open(p)))   # noqa: E731
E4 = {(r["workload"], r["arm"]): r for r in rd("results/analysis/gate_e/e4/mechanism.csv")}
E5 = {(r["threshold"], r["arm"]): r for r in rd("results/analysis/gate_e/e5/mechanism.csv")}
DIST = {"stencil": 1125000, "graphbfs": 287956}   # tests/e4_analyze.py:27, e5_analyze.py:35 (distinct 4 KB pages touched)
F = lambda r, k: float(r[k])   # noqa: E731
def decomp(r0, r7):
    f0, f7, d0, d7 = F(r0, "demand_faults"), F(r7, "demand_faults"), F(r0, "d5_s"), F(r7, "d5_s")
    p0, p7 = d0 / f0, d7 / f7
    cost = f7 * p0
    return dict(f0=f0, f7=f7, d0=d0, d7=d7, p0=p0, p7=p7, cost=cost, red=d0 - d7, cnt=(f0 - f7) * p0, per=f7 * (p0 - p7))
rows = [("E4 Stencil-24K, C0 vs C7-W512 (t51)", "E4.mech.stencil.C0 / E4.mech.stencil.C7-W512", decomp(E4[("stencil", "C0")], E4[("stencil", "C7-W512")])),
        ("E4 GraphBFS-23, C0 vs C7-W512 (t51)", "E4.mech.graphbfs.C0 / E4.mech.graphbfs.C7-W512", decomp(E4[("graphbfs", "C0")], E4[("graphbfs", "C7-W512")])),
        ("E5 Stencil-24K, C0 vs C7W512 (t51)", "E5.mech.t51.C0 / E5.mech.t51.C7W512", decomp(E5[("51", "C0")], E5[("51", "C7W512")]))]
o = ["# C22 VI-1 / VI-2: copy offload against fault reduction (E4 and E5)", "", "Script `tests/c22_vi1_iv4.py`; sources `gate_e/e4/mechanism.csv` and `gate_e/e5/mechanism.csv` (medians of 10 runs per arm; the E4 arms run at the shipped threshold 51 with the E3a-2 module, E5's C0 and C7W512 at t51 likewise, a separate session).", "",
     "## Decomposition of the D5 reduction (C0 -> C7-W512, prefetcher on, t51)", "",
     "Let f0, f7 be the demand faults and r0, r7 the D5 per fault of C0 and C7. D5 reduction = f0 r0 - f7 r7 = (f0 - f7) r0 [fault-count part] + f7 (r0 - r7) [per-fault part].", "",
     "| gate / pair | evidence | faults C0 | faults C7 | D5 C0 (s) | D5 C7 (s) | D5/fault C0 (ns) | D5/fault C7 (ns) | D5 of C7's faults at C0's rate (s) | reduction (s) | fault-count part (s, %) | per-fault part (s, %) |", "|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|"]
for name, ev, d in rows:
    o.append(f"| {name} | `{ev}` | {d['f0']:,.0f} | {d['f7']:,.0f} | {d['d0']:.4f} | {d['d7']:.4f} | {1e9*d['p0']:.1f} | {1e9*d['p7']:.1f} | {d['cost']:.4f} | {d['red']:.4f} | {d['cnt']:.4f} ({100*d['cnt']/d['red']:.1f}%) | {d['per']:.4f} ({100*d['per']/d['red']:.1f}%) |")
o += ["", "Reading: the D5 reduction is mostly the fault-count part (E4 Stencil-24K 85.9%, per-fault part 14.1% with 310 -> 276 ns per fault; E4 GraphBFS-23 99.1%, per-fault D5 unchanged at 1.10 us; E5 Stencil-24K see the row above). Neither is a measurement of copy offload: the per-fault change at t51 is within what the changed fault mix produces (per-fault D5 is not separable from the fault count, CS2-N4). **Prefetch-on D5 totals are not evidence of copy offload**, as CS2-N4 states: the D5 fall tracks the fault fall (E5 D(51) = +0.4009, `E5.D(51)`). Copy offload shows only with the prefetcher off (E4 C6 vs C1 and E5 t100 vs C0-toff; Table V rows 'C1', 'C6-W512', 'C0-toff', 'C7W512-toff': per-fault D5 0.55 -> 0.17 us on Stencil-24K, 0.59 -> 0.21 us at t100).", "",
      "## What `fault_already_resident` counts", "",
      "The counter `g_specasync_fault_already_resident` is incremented in `service_fault_batch_block_locked` (`driver/src-e3a/uvm_gpu_replayable_faults.c:1844`), at `uvm_gpu_replayable_faults.c:2019-2021`, in the loop over the faults of one VA block in a batch: after the check that the page is not already GPU-authorised for the access (`:1986-1990`, otherwise `continue`), `if (uvm_va_block_gpu_state_get(va_block, gpu->id) && uvm_page_mask_test(uvm_va_block_resident_mask_get(va_block, gpu->id, NUMA_NO_NODE), page_index)) atomic_inc(&g_specasync_fault_already_resident);`. So it counts **demand-fault entries that will be serviced although the page is already resident on this GPU** (data there, mapping missing): one count per such fault entry, not per distinct page and not per page staged. Columns `far_frac_distinct` = counter / 1,125,000 (Stencil-24K) or / 287,956 (GraphBFS-23) (`tests/e4_analyze.py:27,122`).", "",
      "## Why it is 2.07% on Stencil-24K when the worker requested 832,392 pages (C7-W512)", "",
      f"- `spec_pages_requested` is **not** a count of pages made resident or of predictions: the worker adds the size of the region it passes to `uvm_va_block_make_resident`, `atomic64_add(uvm_va_block_region_num_pages(sregion), &g_specasync_spec_pages_requested)` (`uvm_gpu_replayable_faults.c:398-401`, in `specasync_worker_fn`, `:324`), once per processed queue item, whether or not the pages were already resident. With W = 512 each item is a 512-page region (`specasync_width_region`, `:293-321`: the W-aligned region containing the predicted page), so requested = items processed x 512: E4 C7-W512 `spec_migrations` {F(E4[('stencil','C7-W512')], 'spec_migrations'):,.1f} x 512 = {F(E4[('stencil','C7-W512')], 'spec_migrations')*512:,.0f} (counter: {F(E4[('stencil','C7-W512')], 'spec_pages_requested'):,.0f}); the other {F(E4[('stencil','C7-W512')], 'lost_after_enqueue'):,.1f} of the {F(E4[('stencil','C7-W512')], 'enqueued'):,.0f} enqueued regions were lost after enqueue.",
      f"- The predictions are first-touch predictions, one per demand fault ({F(E4[('stencil','C7-W512')], 'ft_predictions'):,.0f}); {F(E4[('stencil','C7-W512')], 'ft_same_region'):,.0f} of them fall into one of the last 8 enqueued regions and are suppressed (`:2788-2799`), leaving {F(E4[('stencil','C7-W512')], 'enqueued'):,.0f} regions = {F(E4[('stencil','C7-W512')], 'enqueued')*512:,.0f} pages, about the 1,125,000 distinct pages.",
      f"- The worker's 832,392 pages are therefore **region sizes, and most of those pages are staged after the prefetcher and the demand path have already made them resident or mapped them**: the counter only registers the {F(E4[('stencil','C7-W512')], 'fault_already_resident'):,.0f} demand faults ({100*F(E4[('stencil','C7-W512')], 'fault_already_resident')/F(E4[('stencil','C7-W512')], 'demand_faults'):.1f}% of {F(E4[('stencil','C7-W512')], 'demand_faults'):,.0f} faults; {100*F(E4[('stencil','C7-W512')], 'far_frac_distinct'):.2f}% of the distinct pages) that arrived after the worker had made their page resident and before it was mapped. With the prefetcher on, the demand path maps whole regions at the first fault (`E5.D(51)`: faults fall from {F(E5[('51','C0')], 'demand_faults'):,.0f} to {F(E5[('51','C7W512')], 'demand_faults'):,.0f}), so the worker rarely wins: the 2.07% is the share of distinct pages for which it finished first (E5 C7W512 t51: {100*F(E5[('51','C7W512')], 'far_frac_distinct'):.2f}%, `E5.mech.t51.C7W512`). With the prefetcher off (C6-W512) the same worker finishes first for {100*F(E4[('stencil','C6-W512')], 'far_frac_distinct'):.2f}% (`E4.mech.stencil.C6-W512`) because nothing else brings the pages in.", "",
      "## Which gate each number in Table V (`t_mech`) comes from", "",
      "| Table V rows | gate | evidence ids (`% ` comments in `paper/tables/t_mech.tex`) |", "|---|---|---|",
      "| Stencil-24K: C0, C1, C6-W512, C7-W512 (shipped threshold, E3a-2 module) | **E4** | `E4.mech.stencil.C0`, `.C1`, `.C6-W512`, `.C7-W512` |",
      "| GraphBFS-23: C0, C1, C6-W512, C7-W512 | **E4** | `E4.mech.graphbfs.C0`, `.C1`, `.C6-W512`, `.C7-W512` |",
      "| Stencil-24K, t = 100: C0-toff, C7W512-toff | **E5** | `E5.mech.t100.C0`, `E5.mech.t100.C7W512` |",
      "The E5 t51 rows (`E5.mech.t51.*`) are not in Table V; they are used above only for the E5 decomposition. The C0 and C7 rows of E4 and the t51 rows of E5 are separate sessions (C0 demand faults 339,251 against 339,386; D5 0.1051 against 0.1052 s).", ""]
open("results/analysis/consolidation/C22_VI1_DECOMPOSITION.md", "w").write("\n".join(o))
# -------- IV-4
g6, g7, g1, g61 = E4[("graphbfs", "C6-W512")], E4[("graphbfs", "C7-W512")], E4[("graphbfs", "C6-W1")], E4[("graphbfs", "C7-W1")]
s6 = F(g6, "spec_pages_requested")
n = ["# C22 IV-4: GraphBFS-23 repeated staging", "", "Script `tests/c22_vi1_iv4.py`; sources `gate_e/e4/mechanism.csv` (`E4.mech.graphbfs.*`), `driver/src-e3a/uvm_gpu_replayable_faults.c`, `tests/e4_analyze.py:27` (287,956 distinct pages).", "",
     "## The numbers in Table V (C6-W512, prefetcher off)", "", "| counter | value | meaning |", "|---|---|---|",
     f"| `spec_pages_requested` | {s6:,.0f} | sum of region sizes passed to `uvm_va_block_make_resident` by the worker (`uvm_gpu_replayable_faults.c:398-401`) |",
     f"| `spec_migrations` | {F(g6, 'spec_migrations'):,.0f} | worker items whose `make_resident` returned NV_OK (`uvm_gpu_replayable_faults.c:416-417`) |",
     f"| `enqueued` | {F(g6, 'enqueued'):,.0f} | predictions that passed the last-8-regions filter and were put on the queue |",
     f"| `ft_predictions` / `ft_same_region` | {F(g6, 'ft_predictions'):,.0f} / {F(g6, 'ft_same_region'):,.0f} | first-touch predictions made, and those suppressed because their W-page region equals one of the last 8 enqueued regions (`:2788-2799`) |",
     f"| `fault_already_resident` | {F(g6, 'fault_already_resident'):,.0f} | demand-fault entries on pages already resident on the GPU (`:2019-2021`) |",
     f"| distinct pages touched | {DIST['graphbfs']:,} | `tests/e4_analyze.py:27` |", ""]
n += ["## Can a page be requested more than once? Yes: counts and code", "",
      f"- Requested pages are *region sizes per processed item*, not predictions and not distinct pages: {s6:,.0f} / 512 = {s6/512:,.0f} items, equal within {100*abs(s6/512 - F(g6, 'spec_migrations'))/F(g6, 'spec_migrations'):.2f}% to `spec_migrations` ({F(g6, 'spec_migrations'):,.0f}). The requested total is **{s6/DIST['graphbfs']:.1f}x** the distinct pages.",
      "- The same 512-page region can be enqueued again because the duplicate filter remembers only the **last 8 enqueued regions** (`SPECASYNC_REGION_HISTORY` = 8, `specasync_internal.h:165`; the check at `uvm_gpu_replayable_faults.c:2788-2799`). A region that is no longer among the last 8 is enqueued again whenever another of its pages is predicted (follows from the code); that GraphBFS-23's weakened first-touch table does this much more than Stencil-24K is an inference from the counters (88.7x against 1.00x), not separately measured; the worker then calls `make_resident` on the whole 512-page region (`:398-401`), which does nothing for pages already resident but still adds 512 to the counter. Stencil-24K, in contrast, predicts sequentially, so `ft_same_region` removes " + f"{100*F(E4[('stencil','C6-W512')], 'ft_same_region')/F(E4[('stencil','C6-W512')], 'ft_predictions'):.1f}% of its predictions and requested = {F(E4[('stencil','C6-W512')], 'spec_pages_requested'):,.0f} = its 1,125,000 distinct pages (1.00x).",
      f"- Cursor skips and drops: drops = {F(g6, 'drops'):.0f}; `lost_after_enqueue` = {F(g6, 'lost_after_enqueue'):,.0f} ({100*F(g6, 'lost_after_enqueue')/F(g6, 'enqueued'):.1f}% of the enqueued regions); `ft_predictions` = {F(g6, 'ft_predictions'):,.0f} against {F(g6, 'ft_predictions')/F(g6, 'demand_faults')*100:.1f}% of the {F(g6, 'demand_faults'):,.0f} demand faults (the cursor yields a prediction only for part of the faults: the oracle cursor is weakened, coverage 0.22-0.81 across the C6 arms per CS2-N1).",
      f"- So `pages requested` counts **pages in the regions enqueued and processed (512 per item)**, which is why it is {s6/DIST['graphbfs']:.0f}x the number of distinct pages; it is not a measure of staged working set. At W = 1 (C6-W1) it is {F(g1, 'spec_pages_requested'):,.0f} = one page per migration.", "",
      "## What fraction of the distinct pages did the worker make resident?", "",
      f"The counters cannot give an exact distinct-page fraction: `fault_already_resident` counts fault entries, one per page serviced while already resident, and a page may fault more than once. As an upper bound on the distinct pages made resident ahead of their fault: `far_frac_distinct` = {F(g6, 'fault_already_resident'):,.0f} / {DIST['graphbfs']:,} = **{100*F(g6, 'far_frac_distinct'):.1f}%** (C6-W512; C6-W1: {100*F(g1, 'far_frac_distinct'):.1f}%; C7-W512: {100*F(g7, 'far_frac_distinct'):.2f}%; C7-W1: {100*F(g61, 'far_frac_distinct'):.2f}%). Pages staged but never faulted afterwards (mapped by the prefetcher, or never touched) are not counted either, so the true staged set could be larger than this fraction.", "",
      "## Reconciling with Section IV: \"the graph oracle stages only part of the working set\"", "",
      f"The sentence is consistent with the counters: with the prefetcher off and W = 512 the worker made at most {100*F(g6, 'far_frac_distinct'):.0f}% of the distinct pages resident before their fault (against {100*F(E4[('stencil','C6-W512')], 'far_frac_distinct'):.2f}% on Stencil-24K), and with W = 1 only {100*F(g1, 'far_frac_distinct'):.0f}%; and the cursor produced {F(g6, 'ft_predictions'):,.0f} predictions for {F(g6, 'demand_faults'):,.0f} demand faults. The 25.6 million requested pages do not contradict it: they are repeated 512-page region requests ({s6/512:,.0f} of them), not distinct staged pages, and the {F(g6, 'ft_same_region'):,.0f} suppressed predictions show that the last-8-regions filter removes only part of the repetition. Wording suggestion for the table note (not applied): \"pages requested\" counts the pages of every region passed to the migration call, so it exceeds the distinct page count whenever a region is requested more than once.", ""]
open("results/analysis/consolidation/C22_IV4_GRAPHBFS.md", "w").write("\n".join(n))
print("\n".join(o[8:12])); print(n[10][:300])
